s free cash flow are valuable indicators of its operating performance and liquidity.\nL253: Free cash flow is a non-GAAP financial measure and should not be considered in isolation or as a substitute for financial information provided in accordance with GAAP. This non-GAAP financial measure may not be computed in the same manner as similarly titled measures used by other companies.\nL254: The Company expects to continue to incur expenditures similar to the free cash flow financial adjustment described above, and investors should not infer from the Company’s presentation of this non-GAAP financial measure that these expenditures reflect all of the Company's obligations which require cash.\nL255: The following table reconciles the most directly comparable GAAP financial measure to the non-GAAP financial measure.\nL256:    |    | Fourth Quarters Ended  |    | Twelve Months Ended\nL257:    |    | July 3, 2026  |    | June 27, 2025  |    | July 3, 2026  |    | June 27, 2025\nL258: Net cash provided by operating activities  |    | $  | 42,153  |    |    | $  | 38,075  |    |    | $  | 102,388  |    |    | $  | 138,851  |\nL259: Purchases of property and equipment  |    |    | (13,588  | )  |    |    | (4,098  | )  |    |    | (34,301  | )  |    |    | (19,803  | )\nL260: Free cash flow  |    | $  | 28,565  |    |    | $  | 33,977  |    |    | $  | 68,087  |    |    | $  | 119,048  |\nL261:    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |\nL262: Adjusted income and adjusted earnings per share (“adjusted EPS”) are non-GAAP measures for reporting financial performance, exclude the impact of certain items and, therefore, have not been calculated in accordance with GAAP. Management believes that exclusion of these items assists in providing a more complete understanding of the Company’s underlying results and trends and allows for comparability with its peer company index and industry.\nL263: These non-GAAP financial measures may not be computed in the same manner as similarly titled measures used by other companies. The Company uses these measures along with the corresponding GAAP financial measures to manage the Company’s business and to evaluate its performance compared to prior periods and the marketplace.\nL264: The Company defines adjusted income as income before other non-operating adjustments, amortization of intangible assets, restructuring and other charges, impairment of long-lived assets, acquisition, financing and other third party costs, fair value adjustments from purchase accounting, litigation and settlement income and expense, and stock-based and other non-cash compensation expense.\nL265: The impact to income taxes includes the impact to the effective tax rate, current tax provision and deferred tax provision^{(1)}. Adjusted EPS expresses adjusted income on a per share basis using weighted average diluted shares outstanding.\nL266: The following tables reconcile the most directly comparable GAAP financial measures to the non-GAAP financial measures.\nL267:    |    | Fourth Quarters Ended\nL268:    |    | July 3, 2026  |    | June 27, 2025\nL269: Net income and earnings per share  |    | $  | 798  |    |    | $  | 0.01  |    | $  | 16,370  |    |    | $  | 0.27\nL270: Other non-operating adjustments, net  |    |    | 69  |    |    |    |    |    | (4,645  | )  |    |\nL271: Amortization of intangible assets  |    |    | 9,390  |    |    |    |    |    | 10,275  |    |    |\nL272: Restructuring and other charges  |    |    | 348  |    |    |    |    |    | (15  | )  |    |\nL273: Impairment of long-lived assets  |    |    | —  |    |    |    |    |    | —  |    |    |\nL274: Acquisition, financing and other third party costs  |    |    | 1,097  |    |    |    |    |    | 2,126  |    |    |\nL275: Fair value adjustments from purchase accounting  |    |    | 131  |    |    |    |    |    | 131  |    |    |\nL276: Litigation and settlement expense, net  |    |    | 1,820  |    |    |    |    |